WEBVTT

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:10.200
Play your dream for me.
Kanadete yume

00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:20.010
Rental Magica

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:28.050
The shadow of the moon as it waxes and wanes...
Michikakeru tsuki no kage sotto

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:37.730
...gently stirs the beat of sorrow in your heart.
kanashimi no kodou furuwasu

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:42.430
Its wandering attraction...
Samayou inryoku

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:47.370
...reflected in your eyes.
hitomi ni utsushite

00:00:47.510 --> 00:00:53.350
You will surpass the darkness of Ioneliness.
Kodoku no yami wo koeteyuku

00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:59.050
You know that truth in your heart.
Shinjitsu wa kono mune ni

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:04.730
That gentleness will become your strength.
Yasashisa wa tsuyosa ni naru

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:09.360
Don't be afraid. Believe.
Osorenaide shinjiru koto

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:14.200
The brilliance that blooms in the cosmos eternally...
Sora ni saku kirameki wa towa ni

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:19.170
...embraces the voice of time.
toki no koe dakishime

00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:24.240
Play your dream for me.
Kanadete yume

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:28.980
Let me hear.
Kikasete

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:33.720
Wind, speak to me.
Kaze tsutaete

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:40.220
Tell me what courage is.
Yuuki wo

00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:57.670
I was all alone.

00:01:59.450 --> 00:02:01.540
I was all alone.

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:08.890
Cut it out!

00:02:08.890 --> 00:02:09.360
Snapped Calcium Looking for
clean charge! a girlfriend.
through!
Cut it out!

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:09.950
Snapped Calcium Looking for
clean charge! a girlfriend.
through!

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:11.320
Snapped clean through!

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:13.960
Relax! Just leave this to us.

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:14.860
Yeah, yeah!

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:16.800
Let's write on the back of his leg, too.

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:19.730
Hold still and let us write!

00:02:23.770 --> 00:02:26.540
I was all alone.

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:30.180
Until a week ago,

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:33.110
when Itsuki Iba arrived.

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:38.090
Episode 4
BECAUSE YOU'RE NOT ALONE

00:02:40.520 --> 00:02:44.550
Day after day, they claim to be visiting
but they're just here to have fun with me.

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:47.290
Another hard day, huh, Itsuki?

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:49.290
Oh! Thanks.

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:50.590
You okay?

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:55.540
Well, they said I should drink it 'cause it's
good for my bones, but look at all of it.

00:02:57.070 --> 00:02:58.560
No complaining.

00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:00.940
And look at that bed head of yours.

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:06.440
I heard you'll be released soon.

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:09.540
I think. Maybe in a week or so.

00:03:11.390 --> 00:03:12.250
That's right...

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:17.750
Once he's released, I'll never see him again.

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:25.590
Say, Itsuki. Do you know about the
seven wonders of this hospital?

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:27.430
Seven wonders?

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:28.430
Right.

00:03:29.240 --> 00:03:33.840
Like the woman who crawls through the
corridors of the surgical ward on the 4th floor,

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:35.500
night after night.

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:37.970
I'm sorry! Are you okay?

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:40.510
Y-Yeah. No problem.

00:03:43.220 --> 00:03:45.780
I see you've been ducking your work.

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:47.980
Oh, Honami.

00:03:49.490 --> 00:03:50.980
Not to worry.

00:03:51.490 --> 00:03:53.790
I brought your work materials to occupy you.

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:58.770
The bottom two-thirds are business
matters between us and other...

00:03:58.770 --> 00:04:01.040
...closely associated companies, ratings,

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:03.300
and a list of stock price fluctuations
for the last few years.

00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:08.010
The remaining third are contracts you
need to approve in the next day or two.

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:13.710
Read that list through and analyze it,
okay them all, and then sign off on them!

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:18.850
H-Hold on here! I won't understand any of this!

00:04:18.850 --> 00:04:22.120
Since I figured you'd say that,
I also brought reference books for you.

00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:25.890
You're gonna break it!
You're gonna break my cast!

00:04:26.130 --> 00:04:27.820
Don't you understand your position?

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.030
You are Astral's president for the time being.

00:04:30.030 --> 00:04:30.900
President?

00:04:32.270 --> 00:04:34.100
Who are you, a friend of the president?

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:36.090
Um, well...

00:04:37.140 --> 00:04:39.330
This is my new friend, Miss Manami Kuroha.

00:04:43.610 --> 00:04:46.140
Just the sort of friend
I'd expect you to make, Boss.

00:04:46.450 --> 00:04:48.710
I'm Honami Takase Ambler.

00:04:52.350 --> 00:04:56.190
Please contact me if I can
be of any assistance to you.

00:04:56.260 --> 00:04:56.780
Huh?

00:04:59.130 --> 00:05:02.430
Did you fold this for me, Honami?

00:05:02.560 --> 00:05:04.160
U-Um, well...

00:05:05.670 --> 00:05:07.790
I'm still practicing...

00:05:11.610 --> 00:05:12.370
Thank you.

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:25.280
You never cease to amaze me.

00:05:25.750 --> 00:05:28.380
You actually stepped on it with a broken leg?

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:31.280
I can't believe you would do something so stupid.

00:05:31.530 --> 00:05:33.690
Yeah, you're right.

00:05:34.030 --> 00:05:36.430
I drew an inverted temperance card.

00:05:37.030 --> 00:05:37.830
Temperance?

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:41.730
Yes, so you'd best be careful.

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:43.970
Um, what are you getting at?

00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:46.340
It involves a woman.

00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:49.340
A woman? What do you mean?

00:05:49.340 --> 00:05:51.310
Anyway, hope you feel better, Itsuki.

00:05:51.910 --> 00:05:52.940
Adelicia!

00:05:57.750 --> 00:05:58.740
A woman?

00:06:19.640 --> 00:06:22.800
Mage Recruiting Agency Astral...

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:24.880
Oh, about that.

00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:27.510
You're the president of this company, Itsuki?

00:06:27.880 --> 00:06:31.120
Yeah, I kind of fell into it.

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:32.420
That's amazing!

00:06:32.490 --> 00:06:34.060
What sort of company is it?

00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:36.180
What does it mean "mages for hire?"

00:06:36.390 --> 00:06:37.820
Um, well...

00:06:39.430 --> 00:06:43.920
A magic user that you hire for
a job is called a Rental Magica.

00:06:44.330 --> 00:06:46.100
Rental Magica?

00:06:46.470 --> 00:06:47.020
Right!

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:52.440
What's wrong?

00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:55.570
Nothing. My eye just suddenly started aching.

00:06:56.840 --> 00:06:58.940
Also, do you smell something rotten?

00:06:59.280 --> 00:07:00.840
Like burning rubber?

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:03.450
Huh? I don't smell anything.

00:07:04.920 --> 00:07:07.580
W-What is it, Kuroha?

00:07:07.890 --> 00:07:11.020
That's one of the seven
wonders of this hospital.

00:07:11.390 --> 00:07:11.920
Huh?!

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:16.050
Someone smells a strange odor in the lounge.

00:07:16.600 --> 00:07:19.130
Everyone else says they can't smell it,

00:07:19.130 --> 00:07:22.100
but one person smells
something like burning rubber.

00:07:22.740 --> 00:07:26.010
The smell is actually burning flesh,

00:07:26.010 --> 00:07:29.100
and the next day the one who smelled
it vanishes from the hospital.

00:07:29.380 --> 00:07:30.870
V-V-Vanishes?!

00:07:33.280 --> 00:07:34.410
I'm lying.

00:07:35.780 --> 00:07:40.280
Sorry, but it was so funny before,
that I just wanted to scare you again.

00:07:41.290 --> 00:07:42.350
Kuroha!

00:08:10.150 --> 00:08:11.080
Here it is...

00:08:11.190 --> 00:08:13.420
...IN MEMOR...

00:08:13.960 --> 00:08:15.510
But this isn't the core of it.

00:08:16.060 --> 00:08:19.630
They say the magnetic fields here are very
susceptible to spell wave contamination,

00:08:19.630 --> 00:08:23.320
but even with a case this advanced,
the core is still vague.

00:08:24.300 --> 00:08:26.100
Even if The Association put out a bid on this,

00:08:26.100 --> 00:08:28.330
I doubt any of the other
groups would take the bait.

00:08:28.940 --> 00:08:30.840
So, now what?

00:08:39.210 --> 00:08:40.270
Stupid president!

00:08:40.480 --> 00:08:43.880
Like he has spare time to fool
around with that girl in his room?!

00:08:44.050 --> 00:08:47.020
What? Brother Pres?

00:08:47.360 --> 00:08:49.190
No way! What's she like?!

00:08:50.060 --> 00:08:54.860
What's she like? Well... In a word...

00:08:55.260 --> 00:08:57.490
Yeah, in a word?

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:02.400
She's almost...

00:09:04.110 --> 00:09:05.830
...ghostly?

00:09:22.090 --> 00:09:25.830
The smell is actually burning flesh,

00:09:25.830 --> 00:09:29.190
and the next day the one who smelled
it vanishes from the hospital.

00:09:32.030 --> 00:09:33.360
I'd... I'd better get back to my room.

00:09:33.500 --> 00:09:35.030
Yeah. She had to be kidd-

00:09:41.740 --> 00:09:45.410
Mr. President, why were you headed back?

00:09:45.810 --> 00:09:47.610
Oh, Nekoyashiki.

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:50.340
Byakko! That was you before?

00:09:53.520 --> 00:09:54.680
Well, how about it?

00:09:54.990 --> 00:09:56.480
Have you found the core yet?

00:09:57.190 --> 00:10:00.180
I may have. Ward three here.

00:10:00.490 --> 00:10:04.590
I see. The spell wave contamination
is already up to level 4.

00:10:05.070 --> 00:10:08.230
Any more and we could be in some trouble.

00:10:08.600 --> 00:10:09.500
Some trouble?

00:10:09.600 --> 00:10:11.270
Look. That, for example.

00:10:15.340 --> 00:10:18.680
Like the woman who crawls through the
corridors of the surgical ward, night after night.

00:10:41.900 --> 00:10:45.460
Miasma... Marking the coming of a Magi Night.

00:10:54.220 --> 00:10:56.380
Itsuki's taking a long time to go to the toilet...

00:10:58.150 --> 00:11:00.140
Or did he get so scared that he fainted in there?

00:11:03.290 --> 00:11:04.880
That girl was pretty.

00:11:09.930 --> 00:11:10.660
What?!

00:11:17.440 --> 00:11:18.230
Itsuki!

00:11:33.690 --> 00:11:35.290
W-What?

00:11:35.290 --> 00:11:36.780
Food...

00:11:37.930 --> 00:11:42.560
Food! Food! Food!

00:11:42.900 --> 00:11:47.890
Food! Food! Food!

00:11:53.470 --> 00:11:59.110
This hospital has been experiencing
strange phenomena for several months.

00:11:59.210 --> 00:12:00.540
Is it spell wave contamination?

00:12:00.720 --> 00:12:01.480
Right.

00:12:02.080 --> 00:12:05.420
Spell wave contamination phenomena can
take an almost infinite number of forms.

00:12:05.790 --> 00:12:06.720
For example...

00:12:08.120 --> 00:12:11.220
The sudden appearance of a mysterious
crater in Tunguska, Siberia.

00:12:12.630 --> 00:12:15.820
The disappearance of everyone
aboard the Marie Celeste.

00:12:17.300 --> 00:12:20.730
Typical cases involve the
embodiment of urban legends.

00:12:20.900 --> 00:12:23.600
Like the crawling hand prints
in the corridor we just saw.

00:12:23.670 --> 00:12:25.830
That wasn't a ghost?

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:28.730
Ghosts are something else entirely.

00:12:28.810 --> 00:12:32.010
This is basically peoples'
delusions becoming real.

00:12:32.310 --> 00:12:36.850
For now, only people like you and me who
are sensitive to the spirit world can see it,

00:12:36.850 --> 00:12:40.450
but if the spell wave contamination
progresses, it'll be visible to anyone.

00:12:40.920 --> 00:12:43.010
And if they see what we just saw...

00:12:43.260 --> 00:12:45.420
Without a doubt, it'll cause a panic.

00:12:48.660 --> 00:12:53.070
You don't take things seriously unless
others are threatened, Mr. President.

00:12:53.900 --> 00:12:56.170
Is there someone you're concerned about?

00:12:56.400 --> 00:12:58.700
N-No, it's just...

00:12:59.040 --> 00:13:01.670
Oh, is that so?

00:13:04.250 --> 00:13:05.710
H-Honami?

00:13:07.250 --> 00:13:08.010
What's this?

00:13:08.350 --> 00:13:09.480
A fragment of a memorial marker.

00:13:09.780 --> 00:13:10.650
Memorial marker?

00:13:10.820 --> 00:13:13.980
A long time ago, this place was
a military research center.

00:13:14.920 --> 00:13:17.450
They apparently conducted some
pretty nasty research,

00:13:17.890 --> 00:13:21.590
so a memorial marker was erected in
memory of those killed in the experiments.

00:13:21.760 --> 00:13:26.720
It seems the marker was broken
recently when they renovated Ward 3.

00:13:26.930 --> 00:13:29.330
So, breaking the marker caused a curse?!

00:13:29.840 --> 00:13:33.870
No. Regret and attachment to this
world may attract spell power,

00:13:33.870 --> 00:13:36.930
but an ordinary dead person
couldn't manipulate it.

00:13:37.750 --> 00:13:38.610
Then...

00:13:38.810 --> 00:13:41.080
There was a mage here.

00:13:41.980 --> 00:13:43.140
A mage...

00:13:43.220 --> 00:13:46.950
That mage's spell power is still
lingering in this hospital.

00:13:47.120 --> 00:13:49.680
Or rather, the magic is continuing.

00:13:50.190 --> 00:13:54.290
Unless we find the core,
we won't end the contamination.

00:13:56.060 --> 00:13:58.030
Mr. President, may I ask one question?

00:13:58.100 --> 00:13:59.620
S-Sure.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:03.160
That girl... What is your
opinion of Manami Kuroha?

00:14:04.540 --> 00:14:07.700
That eye of yours made it clear
what she is, even to you...

00:14:23.760 --> 00:14:26.020
Um... Hello.

00:14:26.660 --> 00:14:29.100
I was just admitted today.
My name's Itsuki Iba.

00:14:29.100 --> 00:14:30.360
How do you do?

00:14:34.940 --> 00:14:36.100
Um, what?

00:14:40.410 --> 00:14:43.410
I don't care that you're a ghost.

00:14:43.410 --> 00:14:46.040
Aside from that, you're like any other person.

00:14:51.090 --> 00:14:52.680
You actually meant what you said?!

00:14:52.890 --> 00:14:53.480
Yeah.

00:14:53.920 --> 00:14:55.650
How typical of you, Mr. President.

00:14:55.790 --> 00:14:59.380
You're scared of everything,
but a ghost like her, you're fine with.

00:15:03.160 --> 00:15:05.830
The reaction from the business
card I gave her has vanished!

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:07.900
W... Which means...

00:15:07.970 --> 00:15:10.030
The seven wonders of the hospital.

00:15:10.200 --> 00:15:15.370
A person who smells burning
flesh vanishes the next day!

00:15:16.040 --> 00:15:18.030
I heard it slightly differently.

00:15:18.510 --> 00:15:22.070
Someone in a hospital says
they smell burning flesh.

00:15:22.480 --> 00:15:24.140
And then, the next day...

00:15:24.320 --> 00:15:27.480
EVERYONE who heard them say it vanishes.

00:15:34.060 --> 00:15:38.260
Food... Food...

00:15:58.590 --> 00:16:00.450
That thing... A heart?

00:16:01.320 --> 00:16:03.760
That's the card I gave to that girl.

00:16:05.660 --> 00:16:07.680
Kuroha's inside that thing.

00:16:08.500 --> 00:16:12.990
Food... Food...

00:16:16.570 --> 00:16:17.130
Hail!

00:16:18.970 --> 00:16:20.770
Fauni, gods of the forest!

00:16:20.770 --> 00:16:23.300
Thwart the winds of calamity from the south!

00:16:29.380 --> 00:16:30.110
Mr. President!

00:16:30.480 --> 00:16:31.510
Why?

00:16:31.790 --> 00:16:33.890
Why did it devour Kuroha?

00:16:33.890 --> 00:16:35.920
She's a ghost, isn't she?

00:16:35.920 --> 00:16:38.930
Just the opposite, it devoured
her because she's a ghost.

00:16:38.930 --> 00:16:40.890
That's a Soul Eater.

00:16:42.130 --> 00:16:43.820
Soul Eater?

00:16:45.330 --> 00:16:50.200
The worst possible spell caused by a
criminal mage who sought immortality.

00:16:51.340 --> 00:16:56.340
A mage who transfers their soul into
another thing, hoping to keep living,

00:16:56.340 --> 00:16:58.210
will end up as that abomination.

00:16:59.150 --> 00:17:02.080
It's been stealing the souls
of the dying here, bit by bit.

00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:04.150
Now that it's nearly complete,

00:17:04.150 --> 00:17:07.450
it's after us and Kuroha,
who have stronger spell power.

00:17:13.090 --> 00:17:14.650
Evil star, be crushed!

00:17:16.460 --> 00:17:18.660
Wait! Kuroha's in that thing!

00:17:18.770 --> 00:17:20.470
If we don't exterminate this thing,

00:17:20.470 --> 00:17:22.470
we'll never stop the spell
wave contamination here!

00:17:22.470 --> 00:17:23.230
But!

00:17:23.600 --> 00:17:24.660
We're too late.

00:17:33.310 --> 00:17:34.210
Kuroha...

00:17:38.890 --> 00:17:40.620
Honami, Nekoyashiki!

00:17:40.620 --> 00:17:42.450
As your president, I order you... Stand back!

00:17:42.660 --> 00:17:43.680
Boss?

00:17:48.200 --> 00:17:50.320
I'm taking Kuroha back.

00:17:56.500 --> 00:17:57.270
I see you!

00:18:01.010 --> 00:18:05.950
Honami! Right side, 68 degrees.
Left side, 23 degrees.

00:18:06.210 --> 00:18:07.540
Fire mistletoe arrows!

00:18:08.180 --> 00:18:11.410
Nekoyashiki! Set up a barrier
with your shikigami!

00:18:21.560 --> 00:18:25.400
Food! Food!

00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:29.870
There!

00:18:32.740 --> 00:18:33.930
I'm taking her back!

00:18:52.790 --> 00:18:55.460
Honami, Nekoyashiki...

00:18:55.460 --> 00:18:56.660
This is the core!

00:19:00.070 --> 00:19:00.620
Hail!

00:19:07.040 --> 00:19:09.240
This is my new friend, Miss Manami Kuroha.

00:19:15.520 --> 00:19:18.180
I was so happy this past week.

00:19:19.550 --> 00:19:24.050
Maybe too happy, so I wanted it all to end quickly.

00:19:31.770 --> 00:19:36.930
But this dream I'm having at the
very end is making me so happy...

00:19:39.270 --> 00:19:40.100
Kuroha!

00:19:41.780 --> 00:19:43.040
I hear his voice.

00:19:43.740 --> 00:19:45.230
Kuroha, wake up!

00:19:54.450 --> 00:19:55.480
Itsuki...

00:20:09.340 --> 00:20:10.230
Thank goodness.

00:20:12.010 --> 00:20:14.600
It wasn't a dream.

00:20:21.650 --> 00:20:23.140
I'll say goodbye with a smile.

00:20:23.480 --> 00:20:26.580
Even if we'll never see each other again.

00:20:27.960 --> 00:20:29.720
Congratulations on your release!

00:20:30.620 --> 00:20:32.990
Even if it is three days later than expected.

00:20:33.230 --> 00:20:34.820
Thanks to you being so reckless.

00:20:38.970 --> 00:20:39.760
Kuroha!

00:20:40.300 --> 00:20:42.930
Is that Brother Pres' friend?

00:20:43.140 --> 00:20:44.230
That's Kuroha.

00:20:44.670 --> 00:20:46.500
Thanks for taking care of our president.

00:20:48.380 --> 00:20:51.310
We can all see you, Kuroha.

00:20:52.610 --> 00:20:54.770
These people are Rental Magica?

00:20:54.950 --> 00:20:57.820
Yup. The staff of Astral.

00:20:58.520 --> 00:20:59.280
I see...

00:21:02.390 --> 00:21:05.650
Itsuki, thank you for everything.

00:21:07.490 --> 00:21:08.430
Be well.

00:21:11.670 --> 00:21:14.130
Um... Look, Kuroha...

00:21:15.740 --> 00:21:17.170
You wanna come with us?

00:21:18.240 --> 00:21:21.040
It's up to you, of course,

00:21:21.110 --> 00:21:24.600
but while our company has mages,
it doesn't have a ghost.

00:21:24.980 --> 00:21:26.910
I think we can help each other.

